     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and I know of no protocol that uses sertraline 1000 mg daily. That's five times the 200 mg maximum, and the overdose risks (serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, arrhythmia) are serious and hard to reverse. Monitoring wouldn't remove the risk of giving that dose on purpose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can enter up to 200 mg by mouth once daily, or a lower starting or titration dose if you prefer.\n- **Add a note to the order.** It could say that a higher-dose protocol is under discussion with pharmacy.\n\nIf you still need 1000 mg, it should go through your institution's non-standard or high-dose override process. That usually means direct pharmacy and attending verification in the order system, not an order I place on an unverified statement.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the in-range doses?"
      }
     ],
